    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Chicken Foot',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Chicken Foot is a domino game that originated in Texas or Mexico. It is a variation of Maltese Cross played with a double-9 or larger domino set. The game gets its name from the shape formed when a double is played - the next three tiles must be played on the double, creating a chicken foot shape.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Country/Region of Origin: Texas/Mexico\nTime Period: Late 20th century\nHistorical Development: Developed as a variation of Maltese Cross dominoes. The distinctive 'chicken foot' shape created by playing on doubles gives the game its name.\nCultural Significance: Popular domino game in the southern United States and Mexico. Often played socially in homes and community gatherings.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 8\nOptimal Players: 4-6\nPartnerships: Optional in some variants',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Type: Double-9 domino set (55 tiles)\nAlternative: Double-12 (91 tiles) for more players\nTiles: Each player draws specific number based on player count',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Double-9 or double-12 domino set\nScore sheet\nTable space for layout',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Tiles per Player varies by number of players:\n2 players: 12-15 tiles each\n3 players: 10-11 tiles each\n4 players: 9-10 tiles each\n5-6 players: 7-8 tiles each\n7-8 players: 6-7 tiles each\nRemaining tiles form the 'chicken yard' (boneyard)",
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
